ent-MedievalFoodSoupMushroomPurple = purple mushroom soup
    .desc = A soup of purple mushrooms. It looks unusual, but smells good.
ent-MedievalFoodPotatoMashed = mashed potatoes
    .desc = Boiled potatoes mashed into a soft puree.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupWorm = worm soup
    .desc = A thin broth with worms in it. It fools the belly, not the tongue.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupRotten = rotten soup
    .desc = A stew boiled from spoiled meat. It smells terrible. You can eat it, but you will regret it.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupCrab = crab soup
    .desc = A thick soup with pieces of crab.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupFish = fish soup
    .desc = A rich soup of fresh fish and potatoes.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupGarlic = garlic soup
    .desc = A creamy soup with garlic. It wakes you up and smells through the whole tavern.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupCheese = cheese soup
    .desc = A thick soup with melted cheese.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupTomato = tomato soup
    .desc = A bright soup of ripe tomatoes.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupCucumber = cucumber soup
    .desc = A light cucumber soup with a sour touch.
ent-MedievalFoodSoupAppleChicken = apples in chicken broth
    .desc = Chicken broth with apple and orange slices. Sweet, sour and warming.
